<p><strong>A temporary transfer sends a therapist to another branch for a set time: they are locked at their home branch while away, open to bookings again when the time is up, and you can extend the visit or recall them early.</strong></p>
<p><em>The scene below is a typical one, not a single named customer.</em></p>
<h2>The therapist who is booked in two places</h2>
<p>The second branch is fully booked, so a therapist from the main branch goes over for the afternoon. Back at the main branch, the diary still shows her free, and a customer books her for 3 pm. Now two branches are counting on the same person.</p>
<h2>Why it happens</h2>
<ul><li>The move is agreed verbally and never written into the schedule.</li><li>The home branch keeps selling her time.</li><li>If the visit runs long or ends early, nobody updates anything.</li></ul>
<h2>Temporary transfer: locked while away</h2>
<p>With Zennly, you transfer the therapist to the other branch for a set length of time. For that time <strong>she is locked at her home branch</strong>, so nobody can book her there while she is away. When the time is over, <strong>she opens up for bookings at her home branch again</strong>, with nothing to switch back by hand. The branch receiving her gets a notification, so the front desk can plan the day. See <a href="/features/staff-management/">staff scheduling and transfers</a>.</p>
<h2>Plans change: extend or recall</h2>
<p>Visits rarely end exactly on schedule. You can <strong>add extra time</strong> if the other branch still needs her, or <strong>bring her back before the earlier time you set</strong> if she is needed at home. The lock follows the new time either way.</p>
<h2>Permanent transfer</h2>
<p>Sometimes a move is not a visit. Zennly has both temporary and permanent transfers, so a therapist who is moving to a new branch for good is handled as a permanent transfer rather than a long temporary one.</p>
<h2>Attendance and pay follow</h2>
<p>The system also records when staff come in, go out or are absent, and that attendance feeds <a href="/features/payroll/">payroll</a>. Read about <a href="/blog/branch-transfer-notification-staff-attendance-nepal/">transfer notifications and attendance</a>.</p>
<h2>A quick fix you can start today</h2>
<ol><li>Write down every move with the date, the time and the destination branch.</li><li>Stop selling her time at the home branch while she is away.</li><li>Tell the receiving branch before the day starts, and update the time if the visit changes.</li></ol>
